														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1888189">
									

<p>I'll do a small run-through of nitpicks, will edit post.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Title&nbsp;for&nbsp;showing&nbsp;text</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Title&nbsp;for&nbsp;hiding&nbsp;text</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>It's irritating to read a paragraph of strikes out text; either use a collapsible or state that it's the old procedures.</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Once confirmed as an occurrence SCP-1506-1's position is to be monitored and checked against computer</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing a comma here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>No methods have yet been devised to predict when or where instances of 1506 will occur. Application to upgrade to keter denied: procedures 1506-A, 1506-B and 1506-C remain effective.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I see no point in mentioning this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Procedure 1506-D: Following incident 1506 Sigma, any instance of SCP-1506-1 larger than 200 cubic metres in commercial flight paths are cleared for immediate [REDACTED]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How do you kill an SCP by [REDACTED]?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1506 is the designation for the global phenomenon which spontaneously generates instances of SCP-1506-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds silly to me. I would rather have you explain what this phenomenon is first.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Little headway has been made as to the mode of transmission but the most favoured theory is communication of learned behaviour.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There are two types of people: those who like commas, and those who don't. Unfortunately, you're the latter. :(</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Investigation is ongoing into how the spiders communicate. Research on mallos gregalis and other social spiders has been promising but so far no headway has been made.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you told me what the phenomenon was first, then I wouldn't have to read ahead and look back at this to understand it</p>
<blockquote>
<p>By application of multiple varieties of spider silk</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure if there are various types of slide silk. Might want to do some research if you haven't already.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1506-1 exhibits remarkable behaviour as individuals of mutually predatory arachnid species exhibit anomalous cooperation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a jumble of long words.</p>
<ul>
<li>From what I've seen so far, this is a hostile group of cloud spiders, which I actually like. However, how is this not Keter? It's Hostile /and/ uncontained.</li>
<li>Also, the wording of all these sentences sound awkward, try reading them out loud</li>
<li>Commas can be useful.</li>
</ul>
<h2><span>Final Verdict</span></h2>
<p>Concept has potential, but the awkward writing, unrealistic and boring dialogue, and dissapointing execution makes it a downvote. I would get this looked at by more people in the draft forums. Also, You could try and make a hook for this, if you want a higher chance in evoking emotion.</p>
</div>
</div>
