<p>Sky spiders! This successfully gave me the heeby jeebies, so that gets a +1 from me.</p>
<p>The energy drink cover story is clever, and kept me cemented firmly in +1 territory.</p>
<p>My view would be to remove the part about it prefering human prey, unless there was a compelling reason for them to prefer humans. I don't think it needs to be specifically targetting us to be scary, and I would have thought big, dumb, slow cattle in the countryside would be a much more profitable target for them than nimble, smart, tiny humans.</p>
<p>Regarding the containment procedures, I would imagine the Foundation would attempt to capture an instance of SCP-1506-1 and contain it (in a warehouse like structure). Then, if they can confirm they are able to keep the captured instance alive, they would be able to seek and destroy any dangerous instances in the wild. They only need to keep one contained, after all.</p>
<p>Big nets between helicopters for containment. Some kind of air-dropped incendaries/napalm/madeupness for destroying wild instances?</p>
<p>PS: I would suggest taking out the expungement in the aeroplane encounter (and changing the redaction on the flight numbers to black boxes). The Foundation are not squeamish, so I don't think you should hide the gorey stuff. I wanna know the gorey details! Tell us about the plane!</p>
<p>Still an upvote from me.</p>

