<p>Thank you, I'm taking this on board. As I've said elsewhere, I'm planning a major revision now. I did release this far too early, I see in retrospect. I won't make a habit of that. Some of the stuff you dislike was added specifically to answer questions people had when I was showing my sandbox in the chat. I preferred less information for more &quot;oh god spiders could eat me at any moment&quot; horror.</p>
<p>The dialogue was written on the run in regards to criticism I had after it was first posted but I disagree with your opinion, even reading aloud. It feels to me more like a conversation between people who know each other pretty well. I'm not biased or anything&#8230; The bit I dislike most is the last line as it's a bit &quot;beeeeeeeeeeeees&quot; but the information it has is pretty much the point of that log, heat, prey restriction and the idea of spiders crawling all over you. I don't know how to present that better within that kind of log. With a contained instance, that information should be covered with test logs and the conversation obsolete.</p>

